      "body": "## Overview\n\nFix ReplaySSM state shape calculation when the Mamba group count is not divisible by tensor parallel size. Closes #60346.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Pad group count consistently before computing ReplaySSM B-cache shards.\n- Cover non-divisible counts below and above the TP size with shape regression tests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `HF_HOME=/workspace/.setup/hf-home .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/kernels/mamba/test_ssu_dispatch.py -k 'replayssm_physical_ring' -q` — 7 passed.\n- `pre-commit run --files vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/mamba_utils.py tests/kernels/mamba/test_ssu_dispatch.py` — passed.\n- GPU kernel and end-to-end serving validation were unavailable in this CPU-only environment. The regression exercises the state shape calculator directly.\n\n## Details\n\n`append_replayssm_ring` divided the original group count by TP size, which asserted for counts such as one group over two ranks. Conv-state shapes already account for the replicated/padded groups. Reuse that padding for B-cache sizing and compute the padding as the remainder to the next multiple, including when group count exceeds TP size.\n\nDuplicate check immediately before opening: no open PR found for `60346 in:body` or `append_replayssm_ring group sharding`.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Reuses the existing group-padding helper and does not touch core scheduler/runner paths.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Adds a targeted shape regression and documents the CPU-only hardware limit.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Relevant formatting, lint, and type checks passed.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes the issue, root cause, implementation, validation evidence, and limitation.\n</details>\n\n",
